 soon as mimosa  arrived it didn't really fit with the  story's own narrative about gaia's  condition up until that point i know  from the comment section on that video  that people are still debating the  chapter as we speak but thankfully we  can now move beyond this controversy  because the latest chapter switches  gears and takes us to the final battle  against the dark triad the showdown  between yuno and langus on the one side  and xenon and his devil on the other the  battle comes down to this juno needs  language to buy him three minutes that  is how much time juno requires to  prepare a new attack an attack that juno  believes is going to end the fight and  take xenon out in order to carry out  this attack yuno needs that time to  build up his magic power but he can't do  it if he has to keep dealing with  xenon's attacks and that is where  langris comes in langris has to act as a  decoy who will keep xenon busy long  enough for yuno to make his move that  sounds simple enough in theory but in  practice languas is no match for xenon  when it comes to raw power language may  be able to dodge xenon's attacks and  contribute to the battle a bit with  euno's help but the prospect of langris  holding off xenon on his own for three  whole minutes seems like an utterly  impossible task and yet langris knows  that he has no  other choice if he can't be the one to  take xenon out then he has to do his  very best to give yuno an opportunity to  deliver that finishing blow langris  knows that the life of the golden dawn  captain is at stake the sacrifice and  legacy of all of those killed golden  dawn members is also at stake and the  pressure is on juno senses that langris  needs a bit of a pep talk so he reminds  langris that he is the strongest spatial  mage in the clover kingdom and so he  can't let himself lose not even to  someone like xenon now most mages can't  even use their magic inside xenon's  spatial mana domination zone as you will  recall xenon is able to take control of  all the mana within a certain  cube-shaped area and the majority of  mages are helpless against xenon once  they are trapped within his spatial mana  domination zone thankfully there are a  few exceptions one exception are mages  who are loved by mana such as yuno yuno  is able to resist xenon's mana control  and continue fighting even inside his  spatial mana domination zone the second  exception are other spatial magic users  and particularly spatial mages who have  achieved the ability to use mana zone  and so language uses his own spatial  magic monozone to negate the effects of  xenon's spatial domination zone langris  essentially creates his own smaller  spatial magic space within xenon's  larger spatial magic space if that makes  any sense because now that i've said it  i feel like it makes no sense but the  point is as long as language stays  within his own smaller space he can  still use his magic and defend against  xenon's attacks as yuno praises langris  for finding a way to fight back against  xenon langris thinks back to the time  when juno first joined the golden dawn  squad back then langris thought that  yuno was just a cocky and arrogant kid  and he couldn't bear the thought of one  day being surpassed by someone like yuno  however langris now realizes that he  disliked yuno because he reminded him so  much of himself the two of them are  actually very similar and so langris saw  yuno as a rival and as a potential  threat in terms of his own goals and  ambitions meanwhile xenon isn't too  interested in this burgeoning bromance  he is confident that neither language  nor yuno have the kind of magic that  could defeat him and he thinks that his  ultimate victory is just moments away  and i mean xenon has a point langris is  already struggling to keep up his  resistance and he tells yuno to please  hurry up on the bright side langris has  finally realized that juno's confident  attitude was never a threat to the  golden dawn it was never self-indulgent  or harmful to the squad in fact you know  strength confidence and competitiveness  inspired the rest of the squad and drove  them to become stronger langris finally  comes to fully accept yuno as his  teammate and as someone who is driving  the squad forward language then summons  up the courage to tell yuno that he  accepts him as the vice captain of the  golden dawn and while this emotional and  meaningful bro moment is happening  between langris and yuno xenon is  basically like guys guys please i don't  give a damn about your squad or your  bromance i'm way stronger than you are  and in the end power will prevail so  stop wasting my time with this lame  bonding stuff your persistence is futile  and to be honest it's also kind of  cringe i am paraphrasing but that's  pretty much what xenon is thinking and  yet even against these overwhelming odds  and even against a far stronger opponent  langris refuses to give in he lunges at  xenon declaring that he and his comrades  will never stop persisting because they  are the strongest magic knight squad the  golden dawn at this point langris  appears to sustain some serious damage  from xenon's bone magic tentacle things  but his superhuman determination manages  to occupy xenon long enough for uno to  finally make his move with a smirk on  his face yuno reveals a new wind spirit  creation magic spell called the spirit  of urus which allows yuno to manifest a  massive and majestic bow and arrow as  you know aims the arrow at a clearly  worried xenon this intense and  action-packed chapter comes to an end  whoa throughout this entire chapter  xenon's facial expression barely changed  and he didn't seem worried for even a  second but as soon as he saw yuno's new  spell xenon's expression instantly  turned very grave and very worried so  from that alone it is clear that juno's  new spell is incredibly powerful judging  by xenon's expression he must feel that  juno's new spell has the potential to  seriously injure him or maybe even kill  him altogether so it looks like yuno  might have been right he may really be  able to end this battle with one single  attack  but will it really be that easy will you  know really just go all robin hood on  xenon and xenon's just gonna drop dead  from one arrow or is defeating xenon  going to prove to be a bit harder than  that oh and even if xenon is defeated  sometime soon where does the story go  from there as you guys know i've been  saying for a while that the dark triad  are not the true main villains of this  arc and that the real threat are most  likely morris and the highest ranked  devils who emerge from the cliffhoth but  even so the dark triad have been the  primary villains of the story for a long  time so if all three of them are about  to be defeated what happens next  definitely let me know what you guys  think is going to happen next if all  three members of the dark triad are  defeated down in the comments below also  what did you think of language in this  chapter and do you think that he  sustained serious injuries while holding  off xenon he definitely seemed to be  injured there was blood there but this  is black clover and they do have shenron  mimosa now so he'll probably be fine  finally what did you think of yuno's new  robin hood spell and is it really as  strong as it looks let me know down  below if you enjoyed this black clover  video and you want to see more in the  future just leave a like to let me know  it really helps a lot and if you're new  to the channel or maybe you watch our  videos but you just haven't taken the  time to subscribe yet do me a quick  favor and make this the video that you  subscribe and hit that notification bell  to turn on all notifications you really  have to go through the trouble of  subscribing hitting the bell and then  selecting the option that says all if  you don't do that you're still gonna  miss a ton of our videos even if you are  subscribed it's just how yo